G4137.def:
**πληρόω**, -ῶ
[in LXX chiefly for מָלֵא ;]
1. to fill, make full, fill to the full, with accusative;
(a) **of things **: pass. (σαψήνη, φάραγξ), [[Mat.13.48|Mat.13:48]], [[Luk.3.5|Luk.3:5]]" (LXX) ; figuratively, [[Mat.23.32|Mat.23:32]] but chiefly of immaterial things: πᾶσαν χρείαν, [[Php.4.19|Php.4:19]] ἦχος ἐλήρωσε τ. οἶκον, [[Act.2.2|Act.2:2]] with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[Act.5.28|Act.5:28]] pass., before ἐκ, [[Jhn.12.3|Jhn.12:3]] (cf. B1., § 36, 4); π. τ. καρδίαν, [[Jhn.16.6|Jhn.16:6]], [[Act.5.3|Act.5:3]]; metaphorically, of the all-pervading activity of Christ, [[Eph.4.10|Eph.4:10]] mid., [[Eph.1.23|Eph.1:23]]
(b) **of persons**: to fill with, **cause to abound in **: with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[Act.2.28|Act.2:28]] (LXX), [[Rom.15.13|Rom.15:13]] pass., **to be filled with, abound in**: [[Eph.3.19|Eph.3:19]], [[Php.4.18|Php.4:18]]; with genitive of thing(s) (cl.), [[Act.13.52|Act.13:52]], [[Rom.15.14|Rom.15:14]], [[2Ti.1.4|2Ti.1:4]]; with dative (Æsch., al.), [[Luk.2.40|Luk.2:40]] (with genitive, T), [[Rom.1.29|Rom.1:29]], [[2Co.7.4|2Co.7:4]]; with accusative (so in π., see MM, xx), [[Php.1.11|Php.1:11]], [[Col.1.9|Col.1:9]]; before ἐν, [[Eph.5.18|Eph.5:18]], [[Col.2.10|Col.2:10]].
2. **to complete**;
(a) **to complete, fulfil**: of number, [[Rev.6.11|Rev.6:11]], WH, tat.; of time (MM, xx), [[Mrk.1.15|Mrk.1:15]], [[Luk.21.24|Luk.21:24]], [[Jhn.7.8|Jhn.7:8]], [[Act.7.23, 30; 9.23; 24.27|Act.7:23, 30 9:23 24:27]]; ἐυδοκίαν, [[2Th.1.11|2Th.1:11]] τ. χαράν, [[Php.2.2|Php.2:2]] pass., [[Jhn.3.29; 15.11; 16.24; 17.13|Jhn.3:29 15:11 16:24 17:13]], [[1Jn.1.4|1Jn.1:4]], [[2Jn.12|2Jn.12]]; τ. ἔργα, [[Rev.3.2|Rev.3:2]] ἡ ὑπακυή, [[2Co.10.6|2Co.10:6]] τ. πάσχα, [[Luk.22.16|Luk.22:16]]
(b) **to execute, accomplish, carry out to the full**: [[Mat.3.15|Mat.3:15]], [[Luk.7.1; 9.31|Luk.7:1 9:31]], [[Act.12.25; 13.25; 14.26; 19.21|Act.12:25 13:25 14:26 19:21]], [[Rom.8.4; 13.8; 15.19|Rom.8:4 13:8 15:19]], [[Gal.5.14|Gal.5:14]], [[Col.1.25; 4.17|Col.1:25 4:17]], [[Rev.6.11|Rev.6:11]], T, WH, R, mg.;
(with) of sayings, prophecies, etc., **to bring to pass, fulfil**: [[Mat.1.22; 2.15, 17; 2.23; 4.14; 5.17; 8.17; 12.17; 13.35; 21.4; 26.54, 56; 27.9|Mat.1:22 2:15, 17 2:23 4:14 5:17 8:17 12:17 13:35 21:4 26:54, 56 27:9]], [[Mrk.14.49; 15.28|Mrk.14:49 15:28]] (WH, R, txt. om.), [[Luk.1.20; 4.21; 24.44|Luk.1:20 4:21 24:44]], [[Jhn.12.38; 13.18; 15.25; 17.12; 18.9, 32; 19.24, 36|Jhn.12:38 13:18 15:25 17:12 18:9, 32 19:24, 36]], [[Act.1.16; 3.18; 13.27|Act.1:16 3:18 13:27]], [[Jas.2.23|Jas.2:23]] (cf. Lft., Col., 255 ff.).†
(AS)

G4152.def:
**πνευματικός**, -ή, -όν
(πνεῦμα),
1. of or caused by the wind, air or breath (Arist., al.).
2. **spiritual **(opposite to σωματικός, Plut.);
(a) **of created beings **: τὰ π. (RV, the spiritual hosts), [[Eph.6.12|Eph.6:12]] of that which is related to the human spirit, opposite to ψυχικός, [[1Co.15.44; 15.46|1Co.15:44 15:46]];
(b) **of that which belongs to or is actuated by the Divine Spirit**;
α **of persons **: [[1Co.2.15; 3.1; 14.37|1Co.2:15 3:1 14:37]], [[Gal.6.1|Gal.6:1]]; οἶκος π., figuratively, [[1Pe.2.5|1Pe.2:5]]
β **of things **: [[Rom.1.11; 7.14|Rom.1:11 7:14]], [[1Co.2.13; 10.3-4; 12.1; 14.1|1Co.2:13 10:3-4 12:1 14:1]], [[Eph.1.3; 5.19|Eph.1:3 5:19]], [[Col.1.9; 3.16|Col.1:9 3:16]], [[1Pe.2.5|1Pe.2:5]]; opposite to τ. σαρκικά, [[Rom.15.27|Rom.15:27]], [[1Co.9.11|1Co.9:11]].†
_SYN._: ψυχικός, which see, and cf. _DB_, ii, 410, iv, 612 (AS)
